WEBVTT

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:14.790
The Shadow Knight's demand was that 
I remove the barrier before sundown of this day.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.080
He said that if I refused, 
my sister would die!

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.180
This evening, huh?

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.510
We'll need to hurry.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:21.930
Where is he?

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.610
There.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.640
My sister, Runa, is there, as well.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.840
Got it.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.020
Leave the rest to us.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.490
I must accompany—

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:34.360
If he realizes you've broken the deal, 
he might harm the hostage.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.810
I know you're worried, 
but could you wait here for us?

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.740
Of course! I believe you worthy of my trust.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.380
I beg of you, fight well.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:47.940
That's him.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:09.880
<b>Beast Tamer</b>

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.000
The Captive Fairy

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.000
The Captive Fairy

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.500
Just like we planned it, okay?

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.240
Yes!

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.000
Of course!

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.030
Three!

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:32.940
Two!

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:33.460
One!

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:34.460
Go!

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:36.880
Fireball!

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.980
Whoever you are, know this...

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.310
Spells are useless against me!

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.730
Yeah, we know!

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:53.770
They still draw your attention just fine!

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.520
That didn't take him down?

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.280
Such power...

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.960
Might you be the Hero?

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:02.320
Don't insult me like that.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.870
Yet you challenge me, 
aware that I am of the Demon King's army?

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.380
What is your purpose here?

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.020
I don't have to tell you that.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.750
I see.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.170
It was that fairy's request, was it?

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.090
I must punish such betrayal!

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.310
I think I'd rather you didn't!

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:28.270
Tania!

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.620
Rein! I have her, safe and sound!

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.270
Sure! Great work, Tania!

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.730
Just dispose of that 
brute already, would you?

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:42.320
You will not escape!

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.600
But don't forget...

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.220
...about us!

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.520
You and I distract him 
while Tania makes the save.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:53.830
Your plan worked perfectly!

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:54.940
Yeah.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:55.910
Although...

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.180
He's still not down?

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.500
Even attacking with Kanade's power?

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.510
I will not be underestimated!

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.250
Not by you insects!

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:15.120
<i>I see why he thought he could 
invade the fairies' village solo...</i>

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.610
<i>Is this the power of the monsters 
who serve the Demon King?</i>

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.440
He's so reckless!

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:25.860
The forest won't survive this.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.700
We can't let this go on.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:29.330
Kanade!

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.250
Yes?

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:31.820
I'll hold him down.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.330
While I do, hit him with everything you've got!

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:35.290
But...

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:37.210
He's really tough!

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.810
I don't think one hit'll do it!

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.500
It will.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.050
I have an idea.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.040
Okay!

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:05.480
Go!

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.780
<i>The ahrbees' paralyzing effect 
might not work on the Shadow Knight.</i>

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.250
<i>But...</i>

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.170
Surrender now.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.780
You have nowhere left to run.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.670
What are these insects?!

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.670
<i>If they can briefly distract him...</i>

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:22.030
Kanade!

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:22.630
Rein!

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:24.550
Get out of my way!

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.260
Now, Kanade!

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:30.890
Respond to my call, and unleash your power!

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:31.880
Boost!

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:37.730
What's going on?

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.450
I feel so strong...

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:40.940
Kanade!

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.330
This cannot... be...

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:13.840
Rein!

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:15.850
Hey, hey! What did you do back there?

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.310
I felt so strong all of a sudden!

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:19.850
Oh, that?

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:23.110
That was a unique tamer spell.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:28.700
Put simply, it temporarily 
increases your natural abilities!

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.590
My abilities?

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:34.620
Yeah. I didn't have the magic 
power to use it before,

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.050
but now I've got Tania's 
magic power behind me!

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:38.990
As reckless as ever, I see.

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:40.080
Tania!

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.610
Who's that?

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:44.020
No need to worry. She's merely unconscious.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:46.800
But, Rein, I have a few things to say to you!

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.960
I was under the impression 
that Boost was a lost spell.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:52.620
How did you manage to learn it?

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.560
What to say to that?

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:56.650
I just learned it in my hometown.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:57.520
Now, now.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:01.480
What matters is, it allowed 
us save Sora's little sister!

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.060
So let's leave that stuff aside...

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:06.530
and strike a victory pose!

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.060
What a ridiculous dance!

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.140
It's my victory dance!

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:14.160
Good morning!

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.470
How do you feel?

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:17.620
Who are... you all?

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.880
Your sister asked us to save you.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:21.790
You're safe now.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:24.820
I see. My sister...

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.870
Runa! Thank goodness!

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:31.370
How grateful I am to see you safe!

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:33.370
Have you been harmed?

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:34.300
I'm fine!

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:40.770
How can I ever thank you for saving Runa?

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.480
Thanks a bunch!

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.030
You don't have to thank me.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.310
I'm just glad she's safe.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:49.960
Oh... but without your aid, 
who knows what might have happened?

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:53.410
Shucks, I mighta been 
in real danger back there!

00:07:53.870 --> 00:08:00.370
I'd bet I'd've been made subject 
to all sorts of nasty business...

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.160
Eh?

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:03.720
Bet yer thinkin' about it, eh?

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:06.600
Bet those male instincts 
of yours are runnin' wild, eh?

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:09.710
Runa! You're being 
utterly outrageous right now!

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:12.970
Aw, Sis, I'm always workin' so hard.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.950
A little outrageous now and then 
is just what the doctor ordered!

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:19.430
It is statements like <i>that</i> to which I object!

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:23.890
<i>They look exactly alike, 
but they really are polar opposites!</i>

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:27.040
<i>Still, I'm glad we were able to save her.</i>

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.860
<i>Sora seems so much happier!</i>

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.220
Isn't this nice?

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.070
Now you can live together again!

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:37.990
I fear, in fact, 
that we must leave this place.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:42.300
Understandable though 
their reaction might have been,

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:45.080
I cannot live with those who would have 
abandoned Runa to her fate.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.200
I wish some distance from them.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.750
I see...

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.130
Be careful, you two.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:54.680
The forest is full of 
nasty monsters like that one.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:58.190
Yeah, I'd rather not do 
the damsel-in-distress thing again...

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:01.240
But we've spent so much time as shut-ins,

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.480
we don't really know a ton 
about the outside world.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.710
Sh-Shut-ins?

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:07.960
Although, I do agree with your concerns...

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.020
Hey, hey! In that case...

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:11.980
How about coming along with us?

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.220
It's gotta mean something 
that we ran into you, right?

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.910
Don't you agree, Tania?

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.090
I suppose I do,

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:24.300
but such decisions 
should really be up to our leader.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:26.750
Are you all right with that, though?

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:29.610
Joining a party with a human in it?

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:36.550
B-But have you not taught me 
that some humans are noble?

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:40.090
Though I may not yet trust other humans...

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:45.480
I do feel that Rein might be 
a worthy companion... and...

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.040
If even Miss Priss here thinks you're worthy,

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:51.530
I don't mind appointin' you our navigator!

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:53.820
Why are you dictating to him?!

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.780
Only if Rein doesn't mind, of course.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.370
Actually, I'd love to have you!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:02.720
Truly?!

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.780
Guess we're best buds now.

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:06.300
But in that case, you must...

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:07.580
...form a contract with us!

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:13.160
It is my understanding that Tania and Kanade 
have both forged a contract with you.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.640
We, too, wish to come to your aid!

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:16.480
Yep!

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.160
Are you serious?

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:20.510
Yes. You have been of 
such service to us, after all...

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.660
<i>Taming... fairies?</i>

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:27.930
<i>Every species gets tamed 
in roughly the same way,</i>

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:32.150
<i>but the structure of the magic power 
I use differs for each one.</i>

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:35.580
<i>I know the structure of animals and insects,</i>

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:37.950
<i>but fairies are a bit outside my ken...</i>

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:41.960
<i>It would be like putting together 
a whole new puzzle.</i>

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:45.240
Giving up before you even try?

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.400
You wouldn't do something 
so unsightly, would you...

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:49.770
my master?

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.040
We know you can do it, Rein!

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:56.550
Well, it won't hurt to try!

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.870
<i>If I build up the wrong magic power 
when forming the contract,</i>

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:17.360
<i>my words won't reach the soul of my target,</i>

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.060
<i>and the contract will fail.</i>

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:23.420
<i>What kind of magic structure should I build?</i>

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:25.220
<i>Think.</i>

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:30.300
<i>The structure of magic 
that will connect to Sora and Runa...</i>

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:46.140
My name is Rein Shroud.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:56.570
In establishing this new contract, 
a bond is formed.

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:02.140
An oath in our hearts, hope in our souls...

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.750
Your power, in my hand.

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:09.360
Speak now your name.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.460
Sora.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:18.300
Runa.

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:43.110
I-Is it complete?

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.570
Yeah, and I think it worked!

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:48.030
Sis! Look at the weird pattern on our hands!

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:51.800
You did it, Rein!

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:53.830
I knew it would work, personally.

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:57.240
<i>It's pretty exhausting, though...</i>

00:12:57.240 --> 00:13:00.080
<i>Contracting two ultimate species at once...</i>

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:06.010
Th-Thanks, you two.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.520
Do you feel well?

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:09.850
Yeah, just a little dizzy.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.040
C'mon, lean on us a little!

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.560
Backin' you up is our job!

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.520
We welcome your future company.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.520
Good to have ya with us!

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:20.140
Master.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.410
Should we really be allowing 
Rein to go on his own?

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:32.120
Is that Hero not a cruel man 
who drove Rein from his party?

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:38.160
I don't exactly like it, 
but Rein did ask us to wait here, so...

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:42.730
I worry that the Hero 
might lash out at us again.

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:46.110
If anything happens to Rein, 
in we go to save him!

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:47.340
I'm in!

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:49.800
Here it is. The Shield of Truth.

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:53.180
What is it?

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:56.320
H-How strange...

00:13:56.320 --> 00:14:01.270
It's only been two days since you 
embarked on the quest, isn't it?

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:03.960
Yeah, and we did it in two days.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.150
Impossible!

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:08.060
It took us over a week, and we never—

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:11.120
Ah, don't tell me! Is that a fake shield?!

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:14.080
If that's what you think, 
go ahead and check it out.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.020
I'll cast appraisal magic on it.

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.300
Please do.

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:25.690
It is genuine!

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:26.460
What?!

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:27.420
It can't be!

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:29.840
How did they do it so quickly?

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:31.690
What's that?

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:33.390
I see a few new faces...

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.970
They look like children, even.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:37.680
That's none of your business.

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:40.400
<i>I had them hide their wings.</i>

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:45.360
<i>If it gets out that there are fairies in a 
human settlement, there could be a panic.</i>

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.460
Now, the reward you promised!

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:50.820
Right to the money talk, eh?

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:58.080
Twenty gold coins, as agreed.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.950
Now the job is complete.

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:00.890
Are we finished?

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:01.800
Yes.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.750
<i>Now I won't have to deal 
with them ever again.</i>

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.460
Wait, Rein.

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.430
Would you like to return to the party?

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.390
What are you saying, Aggath?!

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:16.960
I never gave my permission for that!

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:18.730
Yes, it's my own idea.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:19.980
But you should consider it.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:24.360
Recent circumstances have made it clear 
that we need Rein's help.

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:30.330
And Rein successfully cleared 
the Lost Woods that we struggled with.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:35.980
I'll admit, the scouting stuff 
is a total drag.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:38.170
I'm okay with it, I guess.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:42.710
Considering what likely lies ahead, 
a compromise may be in order.

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:45.220
You can't possibly object, can you, Arios?

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:50.680
How about it?

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:52.930
I can promise good pay and better treatment.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:55.840
We'll welcome you as a comrade once more.

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:58.180
And we can resume our journey.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:02.350
Don't get so hung up 
on the distant past, Rein!

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.000
<i>The distant past?!</i>

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.160
<i>That's not for you to decide!</i>

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:09.290
<i>These people haven't changed at all.</i>

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:10.280
<i>They're exactly the same!</i>

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:13.740
<i>How could I have ever 
viewed them as comrades?</i>

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.520
<i>I was a true fool. I...</i>

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:17.700
Rein!

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:22.620
Enough. Let's go.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:25.330
We're all waiting for you!

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:26.440
Sure.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.290
You're turning me down?

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:35.010
Defeating the Demon King will earn you 
rank, fame, and enormous wealth!

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:37.460
I don't need any of that!

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:39.290
<i>That's right.</i>

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:45.150
<i>What I've wanted 
since those days never changed.</i>

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:48.110
<i>What I really wanted...</i>

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.030
<i>I think...</i>

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:55.910
<i>I've already got it right here.</i>

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.700
What's wrong with him?

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.240
We offered him an invitation and everything!

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:07.020
He's just an ordinary person.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:12.390
He's nothing like us, with our 
lofty mission of defeating the Demon King.

00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:13.670
Are we agreed, Arios?

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.130
Yeah... right.

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:18.220
What a fool.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:21.060
Abandoning his chance for glory...

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:24.140
Well, forget him. Who needs him?

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.370
Indeed.

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:27.150
It was a waste of time to ask.

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:33.320
It hasn't gone away.

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:36.080
<i>The pain of that moment...</i>

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:37.740
<i>No, not just the pain.</i>

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:40.450
<i>The humiliation, the hatred...</i>

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:42.910
<i>It won't go away so easily.</i>

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:45.370
<i>I, the Hero, beaten by that scum...</i>

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.640
I'll erase him.

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:51.530
With my own hands,

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:53.800
I'll erase Rein Shroud!

00:17:56.760 --> 00:18:00.620
Can the Demon King's defeat 
truly come only by the Hero's hands?

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:03.720
Yeah, I've been wonderin' that myself.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.720
What do you think?

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:06.680
Well...

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:13.900
The old legends say that the Demon King 
used his vast powers to control people,

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:16.040
and that no one could turn against him.

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:20.810
The first Hero made a contract 
with the gods to defeat the Demon King

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:22.940
and took their blood into his own body.

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:27.250
Now possessing the power of the gods, 
the Hero defeated the Demon King,

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:31.460
freed the people, 
and brought peace to the world.

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:34.440
That's the Hero legend.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.120
The first Hero was a fine man.

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:38.470
Unlike the current model!

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:44.180
So what's significant is the blood 
of the gods in the Hero's body.

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:48.910
Most people have limits 
on how much they can grow.

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:53.520
No matter how much they train, they'll never 
be strong enough to beat the Demon King.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.550
But the Hero is different.

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:59.460
The divine blood in his body 
removes all limits to his growth.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:04.140
He'll continue to mature 
and increase his strength...

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:08.450
In time, enough to defeat the Demon King.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:10.330
"Limit break."

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:14.290
That's the power needed to defeat 
the Demon King that only the Hero has.

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.750
But that Hero was pretty darn weak!

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:18.560
He is now, yeah.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:20.700
But he'll eventually 
grow stronger without limit,

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.320
strong enough to defeat the Demon King.

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:23.580
If I may.

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:27.320
In that regard, are you not like 
the Hero yourself, Rein?

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:33.150
You forged a contract with Kanade 
and gained the cat spirits' physical prowess,

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:36.820
and forged a contract with Tania 
and gained the dragonoids' magical prowess.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:43.000
And your contract with us means 
you've got fairy magic now, too!

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:47.740
With every contract you forge, 
you have acquired new power and grown stronger.

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:51.870
Yep! And you're already 
way past an ordinary human's limits!

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.290
I can say that much.

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:57.600
Is this not a "limit break" ability, 
akin to the Hero's?

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:58.760
They may be right.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.110
Hey, here's an idea!

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:03.500
What if Rein forged contracts 
with even more ultimate species,

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:05.720
and got stronger and stronger?

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:09.180
Rein might become strong enough 
to beat the Demon King!

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:11.210
That idea's a bit much.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:12.440
I think it's a fine idea, myself.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:15.480
Much better than leaving it 
to that lousy Hero!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.880
Pretty darn good!

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:20.440
I find you far preferable 
to that human, as a savior.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:23.660
You don't want to, Rein?

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:26.120
You don't wanna fight the Demon King?

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:28.330
<i>Fight the Demon King?</i>

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:32.500
<i>That's the goal I was working for 
in my old party...</i>

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:36.960
<i>When they kicked me out, that goal 
and all my responsibilities disappeared.</i>

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:40.920
<i>I'm having a lot of fun with Kanade 
and the others right now.</i>

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:42.570
<i>But...</i>

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:47.890
To be honest, I would do it if I could.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:49.130
In that case...

00:20:49.130 --> 00:20:53.100
But defeating the Demon King 
isn't like our previous jobs.

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:56.440
So many lives are riding on it.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:59.820
It's not a task to be taken on lightly.

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:04.530
I haven't... 
mentally prepared myself for the task.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.220
Sorry.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:10.790
I'm not strong enough to make 
a decision like that on the fly.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:15.250
I've only even made it this far 
because I had your support.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.150
No, we're sorry.

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:19.470
We weren't thinking about 
how you felt at all...

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:20.710
No, it's okay.

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:23.800
I might as well think about it now!

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:26.140
About what it is I should do.

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:28.020
I need to face that.

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:31.470
I can find my answer after that.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:32.470
I do like the sound of that.

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:34.910
I will gladly await your decision!

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:35.770
Same here!

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:36.760
Yeah!

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:41.230
But there's one thing that won't change, 
no matter what answer you give.

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:45.350
The fact that all of us here...

00:21:45.750 --> 00:21:47.160
are with you!

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:49.620
Thank you!

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.580
<i>What should I do next?</i>

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:57.040
<i>What goal should I strive for?</i>

00:21:58.450 --> 00:22:01.870
<i>The time to choose my path</i>

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:03.900
<i>might be drawing closer.</i>

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:39.980
Let's Make Weapons

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:39.140
Next Time: "Let's Make Weapons."
